    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense looks primed for a productive day, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (82.62) and our OF duo of **Andy Pages** (75.64) and **Kyle Tucker** (75.13). **Gunnar Henderson** is the clear priority today; assuming he secures the leadoff spot against Kumar Rocker, his strong SP skill and dynamic platoon advantage make him our highest-floor option. Meanwhile, **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez. **Andy Pages** is particularly intriguing as his score is bolstered by a slow SP delivery, which maximizes our stolen base potential\u2014the most vital component of our strategy\u2014while **Kyle Tucker** remains an elite start despite a modest BvP history. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jackson Merrill** (74.04) also represent high-efficiency plays, with the former enjoying a substantial 15% boost from the SP skill gap against G. Holmes.\n\nWhile the core is strong, we are keeping a close watch on **Miguel Vargas** (54.70). While his projection is solid, the 39% rain risk hanging over his matchup with Joey Cantillo creates a volatile ceiling. On the bench, **Coby Mayo** (46.48) was the most difficult exclusion; he finished just behind **Liam Hicks** (46.47) and **Drake Baldwin** (48.97) in our efficiency modeling. Ultimately, **Coby Mayo** was squeezed out due to a negative platoon split against Rocker and a lower position in the projected order compared to our active catchers. We also opted to sit **Luis Robert Jr.** (41.09) today; despite his raw talent, the combination of a tough matchup against a Jones-led rotation and a significant negative platoon adjustment made him a risky start in a day where we prioritize efficiency over home-run chasing.",
